-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 5: AMICABLE RESOLUTION OF CASES (Rules 1 to 3).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- READING A RESULT.  JUST TRUE: the text says yes on these facts.  JUST FALSE: the text says no in its own words
-- (a flat negative, an "unless", an "if", "where" or "when" that is not met, a number below the minimum the text fixes).
-- NOTHING: the text does not answer (a list not closed, a grant limited by its own wording, a scope limit with no "only",
-- an "unless" that lifts a duty without granting anything).  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Order 3, Rule 2(1) is a caveat on every answer in these Rules and is not threaded as an input.
--
-- "Reasonable grounds" and "a reasonable period of time" are open-textured: each is a plain yes/no input that the person asking supplies.

