§§ `Order 5, Rule 1 -- duty to consider amicable resolution`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:474 | 1. —(1) A party to any proceedings has the duty to consider amicable resolution of the party’s dispute before the commencement and during the course
-- src:474 | of any action or appeal.
@ref O 5 r 1(1) (src:474)
GIVEN `the person is a party to proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 5 r 1(1) the party has the duty to consider amicable resolution of the dispute` MEANS
    IF `the person is a party to proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of "A party to any proceedings"

-- src:474 | 1. —(1) A party to any proceedings has the duty to consider amicable resolution of the party’s dispute before the commencement and during the course
-- src:474 | of any action or appeal.
