GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 5 r 2(1) the offer or rejection is in writing as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is an offer of amicable resolution or a rejection of one`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the requirement is for "An offer of amicable resolution and any rejection"
        IF `it is in writing`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An offer of amicable resolution and any rejection must be in writing"

-- "at least 14 days": a minimum length of time, not a deadline counted from a date, so it is a number of days the offer stays open.
-- src:478 | (2) An offer of amicable resolution must be open for acceptance within a reasonable period of time and in any case, for at least 14 days, unless the
-- src:478 | parties otherwise agree.
@ref O 5 r 2(2) (src:478)
`o 5 r 2(2) the least number of days an offer must be open for acceptance` MEANS 14

-- src:478 | (2) An offer of amicable resolution must be open for acceptance within a reasonable period of time and in any case, for at least 14 days, unless the
-- src:478 | parties otherwise agree.
@ref O 5 r 2(2) (src:478)
GIVEN `the parties otherwise agree` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days the offer is open for acceptance` IS A NUMBER
      `the period is a reasonable period of time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 5 r 2(2) the offer is open for acceptance as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the parties otherwise agree`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "unless the parties otherwise agree" lifts the requirement and does not say what then applies
        IF `the period is a reasonable period of time` AND `the number of days the offer is open for acceptance` AT LEAST `o 5 r 2(2) the least number of days an offer must be open for acceptance`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be open for acceptance within a reasonable period of time and in any case, for at least 14 days"

-- An "until" bar (ruling of 2026-11-05 (d)): the terms may not be relied on or made known to the Court until the Court has determined
-- the merits and is dealing with costs.  JUST TRUE = the bar still holds; JUST FALSE = the bar has lifted; the function never says the terms have been relied on.
-- src:479 | (3) The terms of an offer that has been made and not accepted must not be relied upon or made known to the Court until after the Court has determined
-- src:479 | the merits of the action or appeal and is dealing with the issue of costs.
@ref O 5 r 2(3) (src:479)
GIVEN `an offer has been made and not accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has determined the merits of the action or appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is dealing with the issue of costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 5 r 2(3) the terms cannot yet be relied upon or made known to the Court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an offer has been made and not accepted`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is of "The terms of an offer that has been made and not accepted"
        IF `the Court has determined the merits of the action or appeal` AND `the Court is dealing with the issue of costs`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until after the Court has determined the merits of the action or appeal and is dealing with the issue of costs" (the bar has lifted)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:480 | (4) Any offer of amicable resolution which does not state an expiry date expires once the Court has determined the merits of the action or appeal to
-- src:480 | which it relates unless the offeror has stated otherwise.
@ref O 5 r 2(4) (src:480)
GIVEN `the offer states an expiry date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has determined the merits of the action or appeal to which it relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offeror has stated otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 5 r 2(4) the offer has expired under this paragraph` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the offer states an expiry date`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph is of an offer "which does not state an expiry date"
        IF `the offeror has stated otherwise`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "unless the offeror has stated otherwise" lifts the expiry and does not say what then applies
        IF `the Court has determined the merits of the action or appeal to which it relates`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "expires once the Court has determined the merits" ("once" counts as "when")

